    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #297\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to branch `bb/relay-270-review-debt-05-12-validate-the-inbox-c-thr_pvjvy9vcey`.\n\n## Summary\n\nAddressed the outstanding medium-severity code review finding on PR #297. The finding noted that `DateTime.fromISO()` accepts non-calendar-date ISO forms (e.g. `\"2026\"`, `\"2026-W35\"`) as valid, but this is explicitly out of scope per issue #270's own text: *\"tightening it further to reject ISO forms Luxon accepts but that are not calendar dates ... is not part of this issue.\"* Rather than changing behavior beyond the issue's scope, I added a comment in `backend/packages/data/src/inbox/inboxStore.ts` documenting this as a deliberate boundary, not an oversight.\n\nThe remote branch had also picked up an intervening merge from `develop` (bringing in unrelated work, including a new `enqueueJournalInboxRecompute` call in the same function). I merged that in locally — it auto-resolved cleanly, preserving both changes.\n\n## Test plan\n- `pnpm -r run build` — all 7 backend packages build cleanly.\n- `vitest run` (full backend suite, post-merge) — 27 test files, 349 tests, all passing.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
